# Machines that cannot run sys — one name per line.
#
# The Synology has no git, so it cannot keep a copy of this repo. It only ever
# receives logins and never makes any, so all it needs is its authorized_keys.
# Every machine that syncs and is allowed in there writes that file over SSH
# instead, and `sys sync all` does not try to run sys on it.
#
# Bootstrap: one key has to be in place by hand before the first push can
# happen. Add it in DSM (Control Panel ▸ Terminal & SNMP) or with ssh-copy-id.

dwkns-nas
